"about_body" = "SafeWalk uses ten years of crime reports published by the City of Chicago, counting street crimes against people (such as robbery and assault) in public places, not domestic incidents. A forecasting model predicts, for each block and each part of the day, how often such crimes are reported compared with the city average. When you ask for a route, your phone finds a path that keeps walking distance low while passing fewer of the higher-risk blocks. In tests on 2024 data the model had not seen, the Balanced route was about 4% longer and passed about half as many real reported crimes as the shortest route.\n\nReported crime is not the same as all crime, and reporting and policing differ between places. Treat the route as one input to your own judgement.";
"about_sources" = "Data sources and licences";
"about_sources_body" = "City of Chicago Data Portal: crimes (ijzp-q8t2) and street centerlines (pr57-gg9e).\nMap data © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL).\nMap tiles © OpenFreeMap © OpenMapTiles.\nMap rendering by MapLibre.";
"about_model" = "Model %@ · forecast for the week of %@";
"about_feedback" = "Send feedback";
"privacy_body" = "SafeWalk does not collect, store on a server, or share your location, your searches or your trips. Routes are calculated on your phone. The app downloads map tiles and the weekly forecast file, which tells those servers your IP address as any download does. Place search uses Apple's or Google's built-in search on your phone, under their privacy terms.";
"outside_notice" = "SafeWalk covers Chicago only for now";
